  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "LEON is a self-supervised representation learning framework that generates location embeddings by applying Graph Masked Autoencoders to OpenStreetMap amenity distributions mapped over H3 hexagonal grids. Evaluation against benchmark datasets yielded up to a 1.87% accuracy increase in EuroSAT satellite image classification, alongside improvements in predicting housing prices, crime rates, and urban analytics metrics.",
      "why": "This approach demonstrates that structured, generalizable spatial representations can be learned directly from globally available, crowdsourced vector data without relying on labeled targets or imagery."
